Dialogue: 0,0:00:11.17,0:00:13.88,Default,,0,0,0,,A few months\Nafter the execution of Arcadio,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:14.67,0:00:16.96,Default,,0,0,0,,Colonel Aureliano Buendía was captured
Dialogue: 0,0:00:17.04,0:00:19.96,Default,,0,0,0,,just before he reached the border\Nof the western frontier.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:21.38,0:00:25.38,Default,,0,0,0,,Of the 21 men who followed him to war,\Nonly one survived,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:25.96,0:00:27.96,Default,,0,0,0,,Colonel Gerineldo Márquez.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:41.29,0:00:43.92,Default,,0,0,0,,-What happened to your hand?\N-Nothing. It's just a burn.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:44.00,0:00:46.04,Default,,0,0,0,,Aureliano José's all grown up now.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:46.13,0:00:47.76,Default,,0,0,0,,Get back.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:47.83,0:00:49.33,Default,,0,0,0,,-Aureliano!\N-Get back.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:49.42,0:00:51.30,Default,,0,0,0,,-Aureliano!\N-I said get back.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:51.38,0:00:54.17,Default,,0,0,0,,-Where's Magnífico? Huh?\N-Where is our son?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:54.25,0:00:56.00,Default,,0,0,0,,-Where is he?\N-Get back.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:56.08,0:00:58.16,Default,,0,0,0,,-Don't touch me!\N-Get back!
Dialogue: 0,0:00:58.25,0:01:00.88,Default,,0,0,0,,-Hands off! Hands off!\N-Go home, Mother!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:00.96,0:01:04.96,Default,,0,0,0,,Ask the authorities for permission,\Nand come visit me in jail!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:05.04,0:01:06.08,Default,,0,0,0,,Aureliano!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:10.00,0:01:10.96,Default,,0,0,0,,Let go!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:11.04,0:01:12.75,Default,,0,0,0,,Long live Colonel Buendía!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:16.96,0:01:18.96,Default,,0,0,0,,-That's enough!\N-Aureliano!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:19.04,0:01:20.17,Default,,0,0,0,,The party's over now!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:20.88,0:01:23.01,Default,,0,0,0,,There's nothing to see here! Let's go!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:23.08,0:01:25.29,Default,,0,0,0,,Everybody back to your homes!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:32.04,0:01:36.00,Default,,0,0,0,,Colonel Aureliano Buendía's\Nsentence would be carried out in Macondo
Dialogue: 0,0:01:36.08,0:01:37.54,Default,,0,0,0,,as a lesson to the people.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:40.38,0:01:44.30,Default,,0,0,0,,ONE HUNDRED YEARS OF SOLITUDE
Dialogue: 0,0:01:44.38,0:01:45.46,Default,,0,0,0,,Ma'am. Ma'am!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:45.54,0:01:47.79,Default,,0,0,0,,I need to see\NColonel Aureliano Buendía. My son.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:47.88,0:01:49.38,Default,,0,0,0,,-Let me in.\N-Ma'am!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:49.46,0:01:51.92,Default,,0,0,0,,-Captain! I said let me in!\N-Get back now!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:52.00,0:01:53.25,Default,,0,0,0,,She can come in!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:04.83,0:02:06.21,Default,,0,0,0,,I want to see my son,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:07.29,0:02:09.21,Default,,0,0,0,,Colonel Aureliano Buendía.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:10.21,0:02:11.04,Default,,0,0,0,,Sorry,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:12.58,0:02:15.96,Default,,0,0,0,,are you referring to "Mister" Buendía?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:17.13,0:02:18.21,Default,,0,0,0,,Whatever you say.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:19.04,0:02:20.37,Default,,0,0,0,,Just let me see Aureliano.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:21.13,0:02:24.55,Default,,0,0,0,,We're just waiting for the government\Nto ratify his official sentence.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:29.25,0:02:30.29,Default,,0,0,0,,What sentence?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:32.96,0:02:34.04,Default,,0,0,0,,The death penalty.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:36.83,0:02:40.46,Default,,0,0,0,,Meanwhile,\Nhe's to stay in complete isolation.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:43.00,0:02:44.88,Default,,0,0,0,,There's no way I'm not seeing my son.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:47.63,0:02:50.84,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm going inside, so shoot me\Nif that's the order you were given.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:54.42,0:02:55.63,Default,,0,0,0,,Take her.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:30.08,0:03:33.29,Default,,0,0,0,,I haven't told you this,\Nbut Arcadio named his baby Remedios.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:37.21,0:03:38.96,Default,,0,0,0,,He wanted to name her Úrsula, but
Dialogue: 0,0:03:40.38,0:03:42.26,Default,,0,0,0,,that name comes with great suffering.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:47.42,0:03:49.09,Default,,0,0,0,,You never told me any of this.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:50.00,0:03:51.21,Default,,0,0,0,,But I already knew.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:54.54,0:03:57.04,Default,,0,0,0,,You were born with your eyes wide open…
Dialogue: 0,0:04:02.00,0:04:03.29,Default,,0,0,0,,looking all around…
Dialogue: 0,0:04:05.38,0:04:07.55,Default,,0,0,0,,so curious yet so unbothered.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:09.17,0:04:10.46,Default,,0,0,0,,I haven't forgotten that.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:14.17,0:04:16.71,Default,,0,0,0,,And I haven't forgotten\Nthe sadness in your face…
Dialogue: 0,0:04:18.46,0:04:20.67,Default,,0,0,0,,…when you saw me return\Nwithout your brother…
Dialogue: 0,0:04:23.29,0:04:25.54,Default,,0,0,0,,after I left you and Amaranta behind.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:31.42,0:04:33.42,Default,,0,0,0,,That image of you still breaks my heart.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:38.92,0:04:41.42,Default,,0,0,0,,I feel like I've already\Nlived through all of this.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:46.33,0:04:48.00,Default,,0,0,0,,But I can't see my own death.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:49.46,0:04:51.92,Default,,0,0,0,,As if the omens have abandoned me\Nfor some reason.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:56.21,0:04:58.67,Default,,0,0,0,,I have something for you.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:03.38,0:05:05.63,Default,,0,0,0,,These are the poems I wrote for Remedios.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:06.42,0:05:07.30,Default,,0,0,0,,Promise me…
Dialogue: 0,0:05:09.38,0:05:10.51,Default,,0,0,0,,that you'll burn them.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:12.58,0:05:14.25,Default,,0,0,0,,I don't want anyone to read them.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:22.67,0:05:24.17,Default,,0,0,0,,Time's up! Let's go!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:36.21,0:05:37.21,Default,,0,0,0,,Don't say goodbye.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:40.00,0:05:43.96,Default,,0,0,0,,Don't beg anyone\Nor humiliate yourself for me.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:45.08,0:05:46.16,Default,,0,0,0,,This is a war.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:48.50,0:05:52.21,Default,,0,0,0,,Instead, you should act\Nas if I was executed ages ago.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:22.92,0:06:25.63,Default,,0,0,0,,Interested in having\Na bit of fun tonight, Captain?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:33.08,0:06:34.08,Default,,0,0,0,,Good evening.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:37.71,0:06:38.96,Default,,0,0,0,,Good evening.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:54.38,0:06:55.38,Default,,0,0,0,,So you know, sir,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:55.46,0:06:57.25,Default,,0,0,0,,we didn't come here after anyone.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:58.50,0:07:01.04,Default,,0,0,0,,My fellow officers and I\Nsimply want a drink
Dialogue: 0,0:07:02.17,0:07:03.55,Default,,0,0,0,,and to have a good time.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:09.21,0:07:12.63,Default,,0,0,0,,No one wants to lie with\Na man on death row, Captain Carnicero.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:14.25,0:07:15.29,Default,,0,0,0,,It's bad luck.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:15.38,0:07:17.59,Default,,0,0,0,,The only ones on death row are the rebels.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:20.71,0:07:21.59,Default,,0,0,0,,Maybe.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:24.33,0:07:25.87,Default,,0,0,0,,But the whole town knows
Dialogue: 0,0:07:26.88,0:07:30.13,Default,,0,0,0,,that the officer who executes\NColonel Aureliano Buendía,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:31.21,0:07:33.42,Default,,0,0,0,,as well as every soldier in his platoon,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:34.38,0:07:35.42,Default,,0,0,0,,one by one…
Dialogue: 0,0:07:38.04,0:07:41.42,Default,,0,0,0,,will be killed sooner or later,\Nwithout exception.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:43.13,0:07:45.34,Default,,0,0,0,,Even if they run\Nto the far corners of the earth.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:02.63,0:08:03.46,Default,,0,0,0,,Well…
Dialogue: 0,0:08:06.17,0:08:08.30,Default,,0,0,0,,Look, I have nothing against the colonel.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:10.83,0:08:12.62,Default,,0,0,0,,In fact, I admire his bravery.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:14.17,0:08:16.25,Default,,0,0,0,,But, unfortunately, if we are ordered to,
Dialogue: 0,0:08:17.96,0:08:19.54,Default,,0,0,0,,we'll be forced to execute him.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:21.58,0:08:22.62,Default,,0,0,0,,That is our duty.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:34.13,0:08:34.96,Default,,0,0,0,,Pray then.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:39.21,0:08:41.46,Default,,0,0,0,,Pray that you never receive that order.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:35.29,0:09:36.62,Default,,0,0,0,,Pardon me, Captain.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:42.54,0:09:43.37,Default,,0,0,0,,That it?
Dialogue: 0,0:10:01.25,0:10:02.54,Default,,0,0,0,,Gerineldo Márquez…
Dialogue: 0,0:10:04.63,0:10:07.26,Default,,0,0,0,,you've been sentenced\Nto spend seven years in prison.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:30.04,0:10:32.58,Default,,0,0,0,,It looks like\Nyou and I weren't as fortunate.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:32.67,0:10:35.00,Default,,0,0,0,,You have been sentenced\Nto death for rebellion.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:36.67,0:10:40.30,Default,,0,0,0,,The telegram orders your execution\Nto take place immediately.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:41.42,0:10:43.00,Default,,0,0,0,,That's truly wonderful news.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:45.08,0:10:47.33,Default,,0,0,0,,We have our first telegraph in Macondo.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:29.92,0:11:32.59,Default,,0,0,0,,He did not\Nfeel fear or nostalgia,
Dialogue: 0,0:11:32.67,0:11:35.42,Default,,0,0,0,,but rage at the thought\Nthat his artful death
Dialogue: 0,0:11:35.50,0:11:40.04,Default,,0,0,0,,would not allow him to see the end\Nof the many things he had left unfinished.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:09.13,0:12:10.96,Default,,0,0,0,,Any last words, Colonel Buendía?
Dialogue: 0,0:12:12.83,0:12:15.21,Default,,0,0,0,,As he faced the firing squad,
Dialogue: 0,0:12:15.29,0:12:17.29,Default,,0,0,0,,Colonel Aureliano Buendía
Dialogue: 0,0:12:17.38,0:12:19.92,Default,,0,0,0,,was to remember that distant afternoon
Dialogue: 0,0:12:20.00,0:12:22.67,Default,,0,0,0,,when his father took him to discover ice.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:23.92,0:12:26.17,Default,,0,0,0,,He saw himself again as a child
Dialogue: 0,0:12:26.25,0:12:28.63,Default,,0,0,0,,wearing short pants\Nand a tie around his neck.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:31.50,0:12:33.46,Default,,0,0,0,,And he thought of José Arcadio Buendía,
Dialogue: 0,0:12:34.21,0:12:36.46,Default,,0,0,0,,who at that moment was thinking about him,
Dialogue: 0,0:12:37.00,0:12:39.13,Default,,0,0,0,,under the somber dawn\Nof the chestnut tree.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:54.67,0:12:55.55,Default,,0,0,0,,Soldiers.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:56.79,0:12:57.79,Default,,0,0,0,,Prepare.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:08.50,0:13:09.58,Default,,0,0,0,,Aim your guns.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:57.46,0:13:58.46,Default,,0,0,0,,Hold your fire.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:01.58,0:14:02.41,Default,,0,0,0,,Soldiers,
Dialogue: 0,0:14:03.04,0:14:04.33,Default,,0,0,0,,put down your weapons.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:09.13,0:14:11.13,Default,,0,0,0,,You were sent here by Divine Providence.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:16.08,0:14:16.91,Default,,0,0,0,,Release him!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:21.08,0:14:22.33,Default,,0,0,0,,Just do it!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:46.71,0:14:49.00,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm at your service, Colonel Buendía.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:02.63,0:15:04.76,Default,,0,0,0,,Welcome to the revolution, Carnicero.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:21.58,0:15:24.46,Default,,0,0,0,,So, I guess it turns out\Nthat you're Divine Providence.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:26.54,0:15:27.42,Default,,0,0,0,,Hmm.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:28.67,0:15:31.05,Default,,0,0,0,,Well, don't you think someone\Nhad to come rescue you?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:32.67,0:15:34.71,Default,,0,0,0,,-Hmm.\N-Don't get yourself killed again.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:36.38,0:15:37.80,Default,,0,0,0,,I won't save you, Aureliano.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:41.42,0:15:43.63,Default,,0,0,0,,No one ever learned\Nof his involvement
Dialogue: 0,0:15:43.71,0:15:45.13,Default,,0,0,0,,in halting the execution.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:05.17,0:16:09.50,Default,,0,0,0,,Captain Roque Carnicero and his men\Nleft town with Colonel Aureliano Buendía,
Dialogue: 0,0:16:09.58,0:16:13.83,Default,,0,0,0,,and they joined the revolutionary forces\Nof Colonel Victoriano Medina.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:23.08,0:16:26.46,Default,,0,0,0,,One year after\NColonel Aureliano Buendía's escape,
Dialogue: 0,0:16:26.54,0:16:29.62,Default,,0,0,0,,the Buendía residence\Nwas once again filled with children.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:32.25,0:16:35.33,Default,,0,0,0,,Úrsula had taken in\NSanta Sofía de la Piedad
Dialogue: 0,0:16:35.42,0:16:37.17,Default,,0,0,0,,and her eldest daughter, Remedios…
Dialogue: 0,0:16:37.25,0:16:39.71,Default,,0,0,0,,How many times\Nhave I told you not to do that?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:40.63,0:16:44.46,Default,,0,0,0,,…and a pair of twins who were born\Nafter the execution of their father,
Dialogue: 0,0:16:44.54,0:16:47.92,Default,,0,0,0,,named Aureliano Segundo\Nand José Arcadio Segundo.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:48.50,0:16:49.67,Default,,0,0,0,,"Sa-tur-day."
Dialogue: 0,0:16:49.75,0:16:50.63,Default,,0,0,0,,"Tha-tur-day."
Dialogue: 0,0:16:51.21,0:16:52.96,Default,,0,0,0,,Let's try that again.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:53.04,0:16:54.67,Default,,0,0,0,,Amaranta took care of them all.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:54.75,0:16:55.58,Default,,0,0,0,,This one?
Dialogue: 0,0:16:55.67,0:16:56.80,Default,,0,0,0,,Listen to this.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:57.79,0:16:59.87,Default,,0,0,0,,"After many years of confrontations,
Dialogue: 0,0:16:59.96,0:17:02.21,Default,,0,0,0,,the government will meet\Nfor the first time
Dialogue: 0,0:17:02.71,0:17:06.42,Default,,0,0,0,,with liberal politicians to discuss\Nthe terms of a potential truce."
Dialogue: 0,0:17:08.00,0:17:08.83,Default,,0,0,0,,Hmm.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:13.38,0:17:15.38,Default,,0,0,0,,You saw it coming, José Arcadio.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:17.54,0:17:21.12,Default,,0,0,0,,You never needed an omen to tell you\Nthat politics are nothing but a plague.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:22.38,0:17:24.55,Default,,0,0,0,,-…Thursday.\N-Good job.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:24.63,0:17:26.84,Default,,0,0,0,,Good morning!\NIt's a bowl!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:35.33,0:17:36.25,Default,,0,0,0,,Where's the rest?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:36.83,0:17:39.54,Default,,0,0,0,,My sons are fighting\Nfor the Liberals in the countryside.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:39.63,0:17:41.71,Default,,0,0,0,,With your brother, Colonel Buendía.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:42.54,0:17:44.12,Default,,0,0,0,,What's that got to do with anything?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:44.63,0:17:47.17,Default,,0,0,0,,Well… it's just the two of us,
Dialogue: 0,0:17:47.25,0:17:49.79,Default,,0,0,0,,and we can't take care\Nof the whole harvest ourselves.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:49.88,0:17:51.92,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm asking you to give me more time, sir.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:58.42,0:17:59.59,Default,,0,0,0,,Tell them to come work
Dialogue: 0,0:18:00.25,0:18:01.58,Default,,0,0,0,,and stop playing soldiers.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:28.08,0:18:29.04,Default,,0,0,0,,Does it hurt?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:33.42,0:18:34.42,Default,,0,0,0,,Yeah.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:49.25,0:18:50.67,Default,,0,0,0,,-Auntie?\N-Mm-hmm?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:50.75,0:18:52.58,Default,,0,0,0,,Please can I sleep with you tonight?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:58.46,0:19:01.25,Default,,0,0,0,,Aureliano José,\Nyou need to get used to sleeping alone.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:01.79,0:19:03.92,Default,,0,0,0,,It's the last time. I promise you.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:06.88,0:19:07.92,Default,,0,0,0,,All right.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:37.17,0:19:39.30,Default,,0,0,0,,Tired of living among the dead,
Dialogue: 0,0:19:40.25,0:19:44.25,Default,,0,0,0,,José Arcadio and Rebeca moved\Nto the house built by Arcadio.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:46.13,0:19:47.67,Default,,0,0,0,,They made it their home,
Dialogue: 0,0:19:48.67,0:19:51.25,Default,,0,0,0,,and continued to love each other freely.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:03.79,0:20:04.62,Default,,0,0,0,,Mm.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:09.67,0:21:11.92,Default,,0,0,0,,All right, let's go again.\NThree times three?
Dialogue: 0,0:21:12.00,0:21:14.88,Default,,0,0,0,,-Three times three…\N-Think about it.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:15.50,0:21:17.71,Default,,0,0,0,,-Nine!\N-Five times two…
Dialogue: 0,0:21:52.50,0:21:55.00,Default,,0,0,0,,Rebeca maintained\Nthat she hadn't seen anything.
Dialogue: 0,0:21:57.75,0:21:59.67,Default,,0,0,0,,It was difficult to believe,
Dialogue: 0,0:21:59.75,0:22:01.83,Default,,0,0,0,,but no other story was more plausible,
Dialogue: 0,0:22:01.92,0:22:05.05,Default,,0,0,0,,as no one could conceive a reason\Nwhy she would murder the man
Dialogue: 0,0:22:05.13,0:22:06.55,Default,,0,0,0,,that had made her happy.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:11.67,0:22:15.21,Default,,0,0,0,,That was perhaps the only mystery\Nin Macondo that was never solved.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:18.54,0:22:21.87,Default,,0,0,0,,Rebeca shut the doors of her house\Nand buried herself alive,
Dialogue: 0,0:22:23.33,0:22:25.54,Default,,0,0,0,,covered with a thick crust of disdain
Dialogue: 0,0:22:25.63,0:22:28.67,Default,,0,0,0,,that no earthly temptation\Nwas ever able to break.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:04.29,0:23:07.42,Default,,0,0,0,,Colonel,\Nthey're waiting for us. Are you all right?
Dialogue: 0,0:23:10.21,0:23:11.84,Default,,0,0,0,,I was thinking about my brother.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:14.46,0:23:17.42,Default,,0,0,0,,Now I know why, for the last two nights,\NI've dreamt of him.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:21.21,0:23:24.09,Default,,0,0,0,,You've all been summoned\Nas the regional leaders you are,
Dialogue: 0,0:23:24.58,0:23:28.50,Default,,0,0,0,,to show your support for the Liberal Party\Nin a crucial day for our country!
Dialogue: 0,0:23:30.63,0:23:34.71,Default,,0,0,0,,The Conservative government…\Nis now open to dialogue.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:36.17,0:23:37.75,Default,,0,0,0,,And we must answer their call!
Dialogue: 0,0:23:37.83,0:23:39.75,Default,,0,0,0,,We should be answering with gunpowder!
Dialogue: 0,0:23:39.83,0:23:41.91,Default,,0,0,0,,-That's right!\N-Yeah!
Dialogue: 0,0:23:42.00,0:23:45.00,Default,,0,0,0,,Everyone, settle down,\Nsettle down, settle down! Please!
Dialogue: 0,0:23:45.08,0:23:48.04,Default,,0,0,0,,Try to understand\Nthat the absolute best way to end this war
Dialogue: 0,0:23:49.13,0:23:50.21,Default,,0,0,0,,is to reach a consensus.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:50.29,0:23:52.00,Default,,0,0,0,,What consensus is that, huh?
Dialogue: 0,0:23:52.08,0:23:54.21,Default,,0,0,0,,Well,\Nwhatever consensus is necessary.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:54.29,0:23:56.12,Default,,0,0,0,,First, we must go to the capital\Nso we can--
Dialogue: 0,0:23:56.21,0:23:57.67,Default,,0,0,0,,For example, to begin with,
Dialogue: 0,0:23:57.75,0:24:00.83,Default,,0,0,0,,the representation\Nof Liberals in Congress is fundamental
Dialogue: 0,0:24:00.92,0:24:03.00,Default,,0,0,0,,as well as in other government offices.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:03.08,0:24:04.79,Default,,0,0,0,,That is what all of you want!
Dialogue: 0,0:24:04.88,0:24:06.59,Default,,0,0,0,,Yeah!
Dialogue: 0,0:24:06.67,0:24:10.05,Default,,0,0,0,,The future of Colombia\Nis what's at stake, all right?
Dialogue: 0,0:24:10.13,0:24:13.17,Default,,0,0,0,,And to reach a negotiation,\Nwe need to stop fighting.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:13.67,0:24:17.09,Default,,0,0,0,,-Like hell we're gonna stop fighting now!\N-What is wrong with these guys?
Dialogue: 0,0:24:17.17,0:24:18.55,Default,,0,0,0,,Have you no sense? Come on!
Dialogue: 0,0:24:20.00,0:24:21.50,Default,,0,0,0,,What's really at stake right now…
Dialogue: 0,0:24:21.58,0:24:22.96,Default,,0,0,0,,Carry on like this!
Dialogue: 0,0:24:24.25,0:24:25.83,Default,,0,0,0,,…is the dignity of our people.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:27.25,0:24:28.92,Default,,0,0,0,,And you cannot negotiate that.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:32.50,0:24:34.42,Default,,0,0,0,,If you sign in favor of an armistice,
Dialogue: 0,0:24:35.25,0:24:38.33,Default,,0,0,0,,we may be able to demand participation\Nin the regional elections…
Dialogue: 0,0:24:39.33,0:24:40.37,Default,,0,0,0,,…for you, sir.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:40.92,0:24:42.00,Default,,0,0,0,,That's right.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:47.54,0:24:48.50,Default,,0,0,0,,Sign here, Colonel.
Dialogue: 0,0:24:57.92,0:24:58.80,Default,,0,0,0,,We'll sign that
Dialogue: 0,0:25:00.17,0:25:02.50,Default,,0,0,0,,when there is more\Nto offer to the Liberals.
Dialogue: 0,0:25:04.38,0:25:07.38,Default,,0,0,0,,But until then,\Nwe will continue with our fight.
Dialogue: 0,0:25:07.46,0:25:08.54,Default,,0,0,0,,That's right.
Dialogue: 0,0:25:09.13,0:25:10.26,Default,,0,0,0,,Stop.
Dialogue: 0,0:25:12.71,0:25:15.04,Default,,0,0,0,,For your support\Nof the Liberal insurgency…
Dialogue: 0,0:25:15.13,0:25:17.96,Default,,0,0,0,,-Hey, I said get back!\N-Please, sir, I beg you! Please!
Dialogue: 0,0:25:18.96,0:25:21.84,Default,,0,0,0,,The Colombian Government\Nsentences you to death!
Dialogue: 0,0:25:23.29,0:25:24.12,Default,,0,0,0,,Prepare!
Dialogue: 0,0:25:26.92,0:25:27.75,Default,,0,0,0,,Aim!
Dialogue: 0,0:25:29.04,0:25:31.00,Default,,0,0,0,,Long live the Liberal Party!
Dialogue: 0,0:25:35.50,0:25:36.33,Default,,0,0,0,,Uh!
Dialogue: 0,0:25:37.67,0:25:38.50,Default,,0,0,0,,Uh!
Dialogue: 0,0:25:39.96,0:25:43.34,Default,,0,0,0,,That is how the legend\Nof Colonel Aureliano Buendía was born.
Dialogue: 0,0:25:43.42,0:25:45.42,Default,,0,0,0,,Long live Coronel Buendía!
Dialogue: 0,0:25:45.50,0:25:47.50,Default,,0,0,0,,Buendía!
Dialogue: 0,0:25:47.58,0:25:52.00,Default,,0,0,0,,HUICÁN'S TOWN HALL
Dialogue: 0,0:25:53.38,0:25:55.42,Default,,0,0,0,,Over the following years,
Dialogue: 0,0:25:55.50,0:25:58.13,Default,,0,0,0,,the colonel armed\Nmore than one thousand men,
Dialogue: 0,0:25:58.21,0:26:00.63,Default,,0,0,0,,and he declared total war\Nagainst the government.
Dialogue: 0,0:26:03.54,0:26:05.29,Default,,0,0,0,,Long live the revolution.
Dialogue: 0,0:26:07.71,0:26:09.29,Default,,0,0,0,,Uh!
Dialogue: 0,0:26:10.71,0:26:11.63,Default,,0,0,0,,Uh!
Dialogue: 0,0:26:17.25,0:26:18.88,Default,,0,0,0,,-Ah!\N-Ah!
Dialogue: 0,0:26:36.13,0:26:36.96,Default,,0,0,0,,Colonel.
Dialogue: 0,0:26:51.38,0:26:54.51,Default,,0,0,0,,What do you mean? I told you guys\Nyou could have those two, okay?
Dialogue: 0,0:26:54.58,0:26:56.00,Default,,0,0,0,,I thought you'd be interested.
Dialogue: 0,0:26:56.08,0:26:57.83,Default,,0,0,0,,Ah, well, I'll drink to that.
Dialogue: 0,0:27:00.42,0:27:03.71,Default,,0,0,0,,This is how they thank us\Nfor leaving our blood on the battlefield.
Dialogue: 0,0:27:03.79,0:27:04.67,Default,,0,0,0,,WANTED, DEAD OR ALIVE
Dialogue: 0,0:27:05.71,0:27:06.54,Default,,0,0,0,,Hmm.
Dialogue: 0,0:27:10.21,0:27:13.67,Default,,0,0,0,,If the Liberals are gonna kneel\Nto those Conservative sons of bitches…
Dialogue: 0,0:27:17.75,0:27:19.58,Default,,0,0,0,,then we're going after them as well.
Dialogue: 0,0:27:30.75,0:27:32.67,Default,,0,0,0,,-May I come in, Colonel?\N-Yes, come in.
Dialogue: 0,0:27:50.96,0:27:52.88,Default,,0,0,0,,You wanna kill me, you son of a bitch?
Dialogue: 0,0:27:53.83,0:27:55.08,Default,,0,0,0,,Ah!
Dialogue: 0,0:28:13.04,0:28:14.17,Default,,0,0,0,,Ah!
Dialogue: 0,0:28:36.38,0:28:37.51,Default,,0,0,0,,Ah!
Dialogue: 0,0:28:37.58,0:28:39.50,Default,,0,0,0,,And so, another war began.
Dialogue: 0,0:28:47.13,0:28:48.17,Default,,0,0,0,,Here, sir.
Dialogue: 0,0:28:48.25,0:28:50.96,Default,,0,0,0,,Colonel Aureliano Buendía's men\Nproclaimed him
Dialogue: 0,0:28:51.04,0:28:53.96,Default,,0,0,0,,Chief of the Revolutionary Forces\Nof the Caribbean,
Dialogue: 0,0:28:54.04,0:28:55.54,Default,,0,0,0,,ranking him as General.
Dialogue: 0,0:28:58.96,0:29:01.42,Default,,0,0,0,,Although he assumed the position,
Dialogue: 0,0:29:01.50,0:29:02.83,Default,,0,0,0,,he would not accept the promotion
Dialogue: 0,0:29:02.92,0:29:05.38,Default,,0,0,0,,until every member\Nof the Conservative regime
Dialogue: 0,0:29:05.46,0:29:06.88,Default,,0,0,0,,was removed from power.
Dialogue: 0,0:29:22.04,0:29:22.87,Default,,0,0,0,,Ah!
Dialogue: 0,0:30:05.33,0:30:06.25,Default,,0,0,0,,Colonel.
Dialogue: 0,0:30:12.29,0:30:14.54,Default,,0,0,0,,Colonel Aureliano Buendía.
Dialogue: 0,0:30:22.88,0:30:24.71,Default,,0,0,0,,General José Raquel Moncada.
Dialogue: 0,0:30:28.04,0:30:30.92,Default,,0,0,0,,All politicians are\Ncomplete shit, Moncada.
Dialogue: 0,0:30:32.13,0:30:35.42,Default,,0,0,0,,The only difference is,\NLiberals go to mass at five o'clock,
Dialogue: 0,0:30:35.96,0:30:38.21,Default,,0,0,0,,and Conservatives go to mass at 8:00.
Dialogue: 0,0:30:40.71,0:30:42.29,Default,,0,0,0,,You're right.
Dialogue: 0,0:30:44.00,0:30:46.96,Default,,0,0,0,,Which is why this war\Nis completely futile.
Dialogue: 0,0:30:47.96,0:30:51.34,Default,,0,0,0,,Other Liberal leaders have already started\Nnegotiating with the government.
Dialogue: 0,0:30:51.83,0:30:53.71,Default,,0,0,0,,And they're about to sign, Aureliano.
Dialogue: 0,0:30:54.96,0:30:56.21,Default,,0,0,0,,Everyone is worn out.
Dialogue: 0,0:30:56.75,0:30:58.21,Default,,0,0,0,,It's been over ten years.
Dialogue: 0,0:30:58.79,0:31:01.12,Default,,0,0,0,,And we'll fight for ten more\Nor however long we have to
Dialogue: 0,0:31:01.21,0:31:03.04,Default,,0,0,0,,for our people to decide their fate.
Dialogue: 0,0:31:04.08,0:31:06.66,Default,,0,0,0,,We've been muzzled for long enough,\Nand we're done.
Dialogue: 0,0:31:06.75,0:31:08.88,Default,,0,0,0,,We both know that you wanna keep fighting
Dialogue: 0,0:31:08.96,0:31:11.29,Default,,0,0,0,,to get even\Nfor what your own party did to you.
Dialogue: 0,0:31:15.46,0:31:16.46,Default,,0,0,0,,That's true.
Dialogue: 0,0:31:17.42,0:31:18.38,Default,,0,0,0,,I won't deny it.
Dialogue: 0,0:31:19.96,0:31:22.29,Default,,0,0,0,,All of those Liberal leaders\Nneed to understand
Dialogue: 0,0:31:22.38,0:31:24.42,Default,,0,0,0,,that our army is legitimate.
Dialogue: 0,0:31:24.50,0:31:26.58,Default,,0,0,0,,Don't confuse our men with bandits.
Dialogue: 0,0:31:26.67,0:31:29.25,Default,,0,0,0,,Then stop attacking\Ninnocent civilians, Aureliano.
Dialogue: 0,0:31:30.25,0:31:32.21,Default,,0,0,0,,You have enemies everywhere now.
Dialogue: 0,0:31:34.71,0:31:36.29,Default,,0,0,0,,Then why are you here, Moncada?
Dialogue: 0,0:31:37.42,0:31:40.46,Default,,0,0,0,,Did they send you here to bribe me?\NOr to intimidate me?
Dialogue: 0,0:31:41.54,0:31:43.17,Default,,0,0,0,,Nobody sent me to do anything.
Dialogue: 0,0:31:44.46,0:31:47.04,Default,,0,0,0,,I just came to say goodbye\Nbecause I quit the fight.
Dialogue: 0,0:31:47.92,0:31:50.46,Default,,0,0,0,,I've been appointed\Ncivil and military chief of Macondo.
Dialogue: 0,0:31:56.88,0:31:58.42,Default,,0,0,0,,I will look after your town.
Dialogue: 0,0:31:59.17,0:32:00.38,Default,,0,0,0,,That, I can promise you.
Dialogue: 0,0:32:01.71,0:32:04.84,Default,,0,0,0,,You're one of the most decent men\NI've ever known, José Raquel.
Dialogue: 0,0:32:07.42,0:32:08.50,Default,,0,0,0,,But unfortunately,
Dialogue: 0,0:32:12.08,0:32:13.50,Default,,0,0,0,,you're still a Conservative.
Dialogue: 0,0:32:24.54,0:32:26.00,Default,,0,0,0,,Breakfast is served!
Dialogue: 0,0:32:28.58,0:32:31.66,Default,,0,0,0,,Aureliano Segundo! José Arcadio Segundo!
Dialogue: 0,0:32:32.29,0:32:34.58,Default,,0,0,0,,The twins were so similar\Nand mischievous,
Dialogue: 0,0:32:34.67,0:32:37.50,Default,,0,0,0,,neither their own mother nor grandmother\Ncould tell them apart.
Dialogue: 0,0:32:38.54,0:32:40.71,Default,,0,0,0,,-Good morning, Grandma.\N-Good morning, Grandma.
Dialogue: 0,0:32:40.79,0:32:43.54,Default,,0,0,0,,Morning.\NSit over there, Aureliano Segundo.
Dialogue: 0,0:32:45.83,0:32:46.91,Default,,0,0,0,,Aureliano José.
Dialogue: 0,0:32:48.21,0:32:49.38,Default,,0,0,0,,Aureliano José!
Dialogue: 0,0:32:50.17,0:32:52.21,Default,,0,0,0,,Just like his father had\Nat his age,
Dialogue: 0,0:32:52.29,0:32:54.83,Default,,0,0,0,,Aureliano José\Nhad quickly grown into a man.
Dialogue: 0,0:32:58.71,0:32:59.59,Default,,0,0,0,,Yes, Grandma?
Dialogue: 0,0:33:00.21,0:33:03.96,Default,,0,0,0,,Go get Remedios and your Aunt Amaranta.\NTheir food is starting to get cold.
Dialogue: 0,0:33:23.96,0:33:26.54,Default,,0,0,0,,Aureliano José felt\Na strange trembling
Dialogue: 0,0:33:26.63,0:33:29.76,Default,,0,0,0,,at the sight of her splendid breasts\Nwith their brown nipples.
Dialogue: 0,0:33:32.92,0:33:34.34,Default,,0,0,0,,He continued to study her,
Dialogue: 0,0:33:35.21,0:33:38.54,Default,,0,0,0,,discovering the miracle of\Nher intimacy inch by inch,
Dialogue: 0,0:33:39.58,0:33:42.37,Default,,0,0,0,,and he felt his skin tingle\Nas he regarded her.
Dialogue: 0,0:34:53.00,0:34:53.83,Default,,0,0,0,,Good afternoon.
Dialogue: 0,0:34:55.42,0:34:57.84,Default,,0,0,0,,Are you Úrsula Iguarán de Buendía?
Dialogue: 0,0:34:59.54,0:35:01.67,Default,,0,0,0,,-Yes.\N-Ma'am.
Dialogue: 0,0:35:01.75,0:35:04.42,Default,,0,0,0,,General José Raquel Moncada.\NAt your service.
Dialogue: 0,0:35:05.79,0:35:06.87,Default,,0,0,0,,How can I help you?
Dialogue: 0,0:35:07.88,0:35:11.38,Default,,0,0,0,,I've been appointed the new\Ncivil and military chief of Macondo.
Dialogue: 0,0:35:11.46,0:35:13.42,Default,,0,0,0,,And it would be\Na very special honor for me
Dialogue: 0,0:35:13.50,0:35:17.25,Default,,0,0,0,,if you would assist me, Mrs. Buendía,\Nin showing me around.
Dialogue: 0,0:35:30.50,0:35:34.00,Default,,0,0,0,,The military forces have caused\Na lot of damage to Macondo, General.
Dialogue: 0,0:35:34.08,0:35:36.08,Default,,0,0,0,,Both the red and the blue.
Dialogue: 0,0:35:36.17,0:35:37.00,Default,,0,0,0,,I know that.
Dialogue: 0,0:35:38.38,0:35:41.84,Default,,0,0,0,,And my mission is to care for the people,\Ndespite the color of their banners.
Dialogue: 0,0:35:41.92,0:35:43.50,Default,,0,0,0,,I promised Colonel Buendía.
Dialogue: 0,0:35:47.92,0:35:49.30,Default,,0,0,0,,Have you talked to my son?
Dialogue: 0,0:35:50.33,0:35:51.16,Default,,0,0,0,,I have.
Dialogue: 0,0:35:52.00,0:35:53.71,Default,,0,0,0,,I met with him before coming here.
Dialogue: 0,0:35:55.88,0:35:56.84,Default,,0,0,0,,Was he captured?
Dialogue: 0,0:35:57.92,0:36:01.17,Default,,0,0,0,,No, he's with his troop,\Nleading the revolutionary army.
Dialogue: 0,0:36:03.63,0:36:04.71,Default,,0,0,0,,He's my enemy though.
Dialogue: 0,0:36:05.21,0:36:06.09,Default,,0,0,0,,Close enemy.
Dialogue: 0,0:36:08.13,0:36:11.26,Default,,0,0,0,,But we have one common enemy\Nthat we hate even more each other.
Dialogue: 0,0:36:12.08,0:36:13.16,Default,,0,0,0,,Injustice.
Dialogue: 0,0:36:13.25,0:36:17.50,Default,,0,0,0,,Injustice is constantly swaying\Nin the direction of what's convenient.
Dialogue: 0,0:36:17.58,0:36:19.41,Default,,0,0,0,,These days,\Nwords are as empty as they were
Dialogue: 0,0:36:19.50,0:36:21.50,Default,,0,0,0,,back in the time of the insomnia plague.
Dialogue: 0,0:36:23.29,0:36:25.71,Default,,0,0,0,,Mrs. Buendía,\NI respect your son,
Dialogue: 0,0:36:27.08,0:36:29.41,Default,,0,0,0,,and I intend to treat Macondo\Nwith the same respect.
Dialogue: 0,0:36:29.50,0:36:30.96,Default,,0,0,0,,That much I can promise you.
Dialogue: 0,0:36:31.79,0:36:33.37,Default,,0,0,0,,Well, I hope you will, General.
Dialogue: 0,0:36:35.79,0:36:38.54,Default,,0,0,0,,Macondo can't bleed anymore\Nfor this endless war.
Dialogue: 0,0:36:39.58,0:36:40.71,Default,,0,0,0,,Have a nice afternoon.
Dialogue: 0,0:37:18.63,0:37:20.76,Default,,0,0,0,,-I didn't hear you.\N-My apologies.
Dialogue: 0,0:37:51.96,0:37:53.34,Default,,0,0,0,,Amaranta?
Dialogue: 0,0:37:55.63,0:37:57.51,Default,,0,0,0,,-Hmm?\N-Where are the candles?
Dialogue: 0,0:37:58.08,0:38:00.21,Default,,0,0,0,,J… just a second. I… I'll get them.
Dialogue: 0,0:38:06.04,0:38:07.83,Default,,0,0,0,,It's all right. She didn't see us.
Dialogue: 0,0:38:09.50,0:38:10.33,Default,,0,0,0,,Not today,
Dialogue: 0,0:38:12.13,0:38:13.88,Default,,0,0,0,,but if we keep this up, she will.
Dialogue: 0,0:38:22.88,0:38:24.42,Default,,0,0,0,,Mother! Here they are.
Dialogue: 0,0:38:25.75,0:38:27.58,Default,,0,0,0,,While Colonel Aureliano Buendía
Dialogue: 0,0:38:27.67,0:38:30.92,Default,,0,0,0,,snuck around the narrow trails\Nof permanent subversion,
Dialogue: 0,0:38:31.00,0:38:34.75,Default,,0,0,0,,General Moncada replaced soldiers\Nwith unarmed policemen,
Dialogue: 0,0:38:34.83,0:38:37.08,Default,,0,0,0,,hoping to foster a trusting environment.
Dialogue: 0,0:38:37.63,0:38:41.55,Default,,0,0,0,,One that made people think of the war\Nas an absurd nightmare of the past.
Dialogue: 0,0:38:42.17,0:38:45.84,Default,,0,0,0,,No banner should ever be above\Nthe dignity of a human being.
Dialogue: 0,0:38:46.54,0:38:49.92,Default,,0,0,0,,That's why the people of Macondo\Nshould all share the same rights.
Dialogue: 0,0:38:50.58,0:38:52.25,Default,,0,0,0,,The same opportunities.
Dialogue: 0,0:38:53.17,0:38:55.25,Default,,0,0,0,,That's always been its founders' wishes.
Dialogue: 0,0:38:56.58,0:39:00.41,Default,,0,0,0,,And the very first step\Nto make it a reality
Dialogue: 0,0:39:01.67,0:39:04.38,Default,,0,0,0,,is guaranteeing public education.
Dialogue: 0,0:39:07.00,0:39:08.25,Default,,0,0,0,,So, as of today,
Dialogue: 0,0:39:09.00,0:39:15.13,Default,,0,0,0,,this space will serve\Nits original purpose once again.
Dialogue: 0,0:39:28.25,0:39:31.42,Default,,0,0,0,,I have to be honest,\NI didn't think you'd keep your promise
Dialogue: 0,0:39:32.92,0:39:35.00,Default,,0,0,0,,or that I would live to see\Nthe Macondo I knew
Dialogue: 0,0:39:35.08,0:39:36.83,Default,,0,0,0,,from the time of José Arcadio again.
Dialogue: 0,0:39:37.33,0:39:39.25,Default,,0,0,0,,What was it like back then?
Dialogue: 0,0:39:39.79,0:39:40.79,Default,,0,0,0,,There were no sides,
Dialogue: 0,0:39:41.75,0:39:42.75,Default,,0,0,0,,no soldiers.
Dialogue: 0,0:39:45.46,0:39:47.25,Default,,0,0,0,,We had no idea what fear was.
Dialogue: 0,0:39:48.75,0:39:51.50,Default,,0,0,0,,And people painted their houses\Nthe way they saw fit.
Dialogue: 0,0:39:54.04,0:39:56.83,Default,,0,0,0,,Well, I'm glad to hear\Nthat we're on the right path.
Dialogue: 0,0:39:57.33,0:39:58.29,Default,,0,0,0,,Yes.
Dialogue: 0,0:40:04.25,0:40:05.67,Default,,0,0,0,,Any news on Aureliano?
Dialogue: 0,0:40:09.50,0:40:10.33,Default,,0,0,0,,No.
Dialogue: 0,0:40:13.04,0:40:15.92,Default,,0,0,0,,I just hope he's considering\Nsurrendering his weapons.
Dialogue: 0,0:40:18.13,0:40:20.34,Default,,0,0,0,,Eventually, men get accustomed to war…
Dialogue: 0,0:40:22.38,0:40:25.05,Default,,0,0,0,,until they can't find their\Nway out of it again.
Dialogue: 0,0:41:23.67,0:41:24.88,Default,,0,0,0,,I'm your aunt.
Dialogue: 0,0:41:24.96,0:41:26.63,Default,,0,0,0,,What we're doing is awful.
Dialogue: 0,0:41:26.71,0:41:28.71,Default,,0,0,0,,No, it's not. It's beautiful.
Dialogue: 0,0:41:39.50,0:41:40.33,Default,,0,0,0,,Get out.
Dialogue: 0,0:41:49.25,0:41:51.92,Default,,0,0,0,,Don't you realize what we're doing?\NThis is forbidden.
Dialogue: 0,0:41:52.50,0:41:53.83,Default,,0,0,0,,Leave me be. Please go.
Dialogue: 0,0:41:56.63,0:41:58.09,Default,,0,0,0,,Is that what you really want?
Dialogue: 0,0:42:01.08,0:42:03.58,Default,,0,0,0,,Tell me to leave you alone again,\Nand I swear I will.
Dialogue: 0,0:42:09.67,0:42:11.84,Default,,0,0,0,,I want you to go as far away as you can.
Dialogue: 0,0:42:16.04,0:42:18.46,Default,,0,0,0,,Then I'd rather go\Nand be killed in the trenches.
Dialogue: 0,0:42:20.13,0:42:22.05,Default,,0,0,0,,It'd be better than your indifference.
Dialogue: 0,0:44:33.79,0:44:35.04,Default,,0,0,0,,Where's your grandfather?
Dialogue: 0,0:44:36.50,0:44:37.54,Default,,0,0,0,,He's right here.
Dialogue: 0,0:44:38.17,0:44:39.75,Default,,0,0,0,,He's been this way all morning.
Dialogue: 0,0:44:55.46,0:44:56.92,Default,,0,0,0,,We've just received a letter.
Dialogue: 0,0:44:57.79,0:44:58.79,Default,,0,0,0,,It's Aureliano.
Dialogue: 0,0:45:17.50,0:45:19.21,Default,,0,0,0,,He says his omens have returned.
Dialogue: 0,0:45:37.79,0:45:39.46,Default,,0,0,0,,We come from water.
Dialogue: 0,0:46:11.08,0:46:16.21,Default,,0,0,0,,ÚRSULA, MOM,\NTAKE GREAT CARE OF DAD
Dialogue: 0,0:46:16.29,0:46:21.54,Default,,0,0,0,,BECAUSE HE IS GOING TO DIE.\NAURELIANO B.
Dialogue: 0,0:46:27.08,0:46:29.54,Default,,0,0,0,,In spite of\Nhis undiminished strength,
Dialogue: 0,0:46:29.63,0:46:32.84,Default,,0,0,0,,José Arcadio Buendía\Nwas in no condition to fight.
Dialogue: 0,0:46:34.00,0:46:37.46,Default,,0,0,0,,That colossal old man,\Nbeaten by the sun and rain,
Dialogue: 0,0:46:38.04,0:46:39.75,Default,,0,0,0,,was indifferent to everything.
Dialogue: 0,0:47:09.88,0:47:11.13,Default,,0,0,0,,We come from water,
Dialogue: 0,0:47:12.88,0:47:15.13,Default,,0,0,0,,and our fates are intertwined.
Dialogue: 0,0:47:19.33,0:47:20.71,Default,,0,0,0,,Try to sleep some, my love.
Dialogue: 0,0:47:23.29,0:47:24.83,Default,,0,0,0,,The afternoon is so beautiful
Dialogue: 0,0:47:26.54,0:47:27.42,Default,,0,0,0,,and cool.
Dialogue: 0,0:48:01.67,0:48:02.71,Default,,0,0,0,,Wait, woman!
Dialogue: 0,0:48:04.63,0:48:06.17,Default,,0,0,0,,Wait, I'm not sleepy yet.
Dialogue: 0,0:48:07.29,0:48:11.71,Default,,0,0,0,,José Arcadio Buendía found\Nconsolation in dreaming of infinite rooms.
Dialogue: 0,0:48:12.25,0:48:14.29,Default,,0,0,0,,He dreamt of getting out of bed,
Dialogue: 0,0:48:15.75,0:48:16.96,Default,,0,0,0,,opening the door,
Dialogue: 0,0:48:17.88,0:48:19.76,Default,,0,0,0,,and entering another room,
Dialogue: 0,0:48:35.67,0:48:36.67,Default,,0,0,0,,My dear boy.
Dialogue: 0,0:49:11.33,0:49:12.41,Default,,0,0,0,,Melquiades,
Dialogue: 0,0:49:14.04,0:49:15.17,Default,,0,0,0,,my dear old friend.
Dialogue: 0,0:49:28.25,0:49:31.92,Default,,0,0,0,,And then another,\Nas if in a gallery of mirrors,
Dialogue: 0,0:49:32.88,0:49:35.63,Default,,0,0,0,,until he came across a descendant of his,
Dialogue: 0,0:49:36.21,0:49:38.00,Default,,0,0,0,,Aureliano Babilonia,
Dialogue: 0,0:49:38.08,0:49:40.29,Default,,0,0,0,,as he read, many years later,
Dialogue: 0,0:49:40.38,0:49:42.76,Default,,0,0,0,,from Melquiades's manuscripts,
Dialogue: 0,0:49:42.83,0:49:46.91,Default,,0,0,0,,about that very same moment\NJosé Arcadio Buendía was living.
Dialogue: 0,0:49:51.63,0:49:52.88,Default,,0,0,0,,Prudencio.
Dialogue: 0,0:50:32.67,0:50:35.67,Default,,0,0,0,,A light rain\Nof tiny, yellow flowers
Dialogue: 0,0:50:35.75,0:50:39.33,Default,,0,0,0,,fell over the town\Nall through the night in a silent storm.
Dialogue: 0,0:50:49.04,0:50:51.58,Default,,0,0,0,,They covered the roofs\Nand blocked the doors.
Dialogue: 0,0:50:56.50,0:50:58.75,Default,,0,0,0,,So many flowers fell from the sky
Dialogue: 0,0:50:58.83,0:51:01.41,Default,,0,0,0,,that they had to\Nclear the streets away with shovels
Dialogue: 0,0:51:01.50,0:51:03.71,Default,,0,0,0,,so the funeral procession\Ncould pass through.
Dialogue: 0,0:52:43.25,0:52:45.46,Default,,0,0,0,,Years\Nafter the death of his father,
Dialogue: 0,0:52:46.33,0:52:48.66,Default,,0,0,0,,at dawn on the first of October,
Dialogue: 0,0:52:48.75,0:52:51.50,Default,,0,0,0,,Colonel Aureliano Buendía\Nreturned to Macondo
Dialogue: 0,0:52:51.58,0:52:53.50,Default,,0,0,0,,with one thousand well-armed men.
Dialogue: 0,0:52:54.13,0:52:57.34,Default,,0,0,0,,The garrison had received orders\Nto resist to the end.
Dialogue: 0,0:52:57.42,0:53:00.34,Default,,0,0,0,,Ladies! Gentlemen!\NPlease go home!
Dialogue: 0,0:53:08.42,0:53:11.09,Default,,0,0,0,,Everyone, close your doors! Stay inside!
Dialogue: 0,0:53:11.17,0:53:14.42,Default,,0,0,0,,Come on! Keep moving!\NBring that cannon to the front!
Dialogue: 0,0:53:16.58,0:53:17.41,Default,,0,0,0,,Very good!
Dialogue: 0,0:53:18.67,0:53:19.63,Default,,0,0,0,,José Raquel!
Dialogue: 0,0:53:20.46,0:53:22.04,Default,,0,0,0,,José Raquel, what's happening?
Dialogue: 0,0:53:22.54,0:53:23.54,Default,,0,0,0,,Aureliano.
Dialogue: 0,0:53:24.04,0:53:25.96,Default,,0,0,0,,He and his men arrived at dawn.
Dialogue: 0,0:53:30.71,0:53:31.67,Default,,0,0,0,,What will you do?
Dialogue: 0,0:53:32.42,0:53:33.38,Default,,0,0,0,,If they attack us,
Dialogue: 0,0:53:33.96,0:53:35.38,Default,,0,0,0,,we will defend ourselves.
Dialogue: 0,0:53:35.96,0:53:39.79,Default,,0,0,0,,Bring the machine gun here!\NTo the front as well! Everyone ready?
Dialogue: 0,0:53:39.88,0:53:42.13,Default,,0,0,0,,I don't know which one of you\Nis the bigger fool here!
Dialogue: 0,0:53:44.63,0:53:50.80,Default,,0,0,0,,PUBLIC SCHOOL
Dialogue: 0,0:54:10.88,0:54:13.51,Default,,0,0,0,,Úrsula felt like\Nher son was a stranger.
Dialogue: 0,0:54:15.83,0:54:18.62,Default,,0,0,0,,His face had acquired a metallic hardness,
Dialogue: 0,0:54:18.71,0:54:22.63,Default,,0,0,0,,and he was showing the first symptoms\Nof resistance to nostalgia.
Dialogue: 0,0:54:28.00,0:54:28.83,Default,,0,0,0,,Aureliano.
Dialogue: 0,0:54:29.88,0:54:30.76,Default,,0,0,0,,Mother.
Dialogue: 0,0:54:34.21,0:54:35.50,Default,,0,0,0,,Will you attack Macondo?
Dialogue: 0,0:54:37.13,0:54:38.46,Default,,0,0,0,,That'd be an atrocity.
Dialogue: 0,0:54:38.96,0:54:40.34,Default,,0,0,0,,There is no other way.
Dialogue: 0,0:54:40.83,0:54:42.79,Default,,0,0,0,,We have to overthrow the government.
Dialogue: 0,0:54:43.75,0:54:45.08,Default,,0,0,0,,Aureliano, my God.
Dialogue: 0,0:54:47.46,0:54:49.92,Default,,0,0,0,,We have had so many years of tranquility.
Dialogue: 0,0:54:52.25,0:54:55.17,Default,,0,0,0,,No one has spoken of parties or banners.
Dialogue: 0,0:54:57.71,0:54:58.84,Default,,0,0,0,,Don't do this, son.
Dialogue: 0,0:55:11.29,0:55:13.58,Default,,0,0,0,,I'll give Moncada the option to surrender.
Dialogue: 0,0:55:14.46,0:55:16.13,Default,,0,0,0,,That's more than enough, I think.
Dialogue: 0,0:55:16.67,0:55:19.25,Default,,0,0,0,,You are the leader of these bandits,\Naren't you?
Dialogue: 0,0:55:19.33,0:55:22.16,Default,,0,0,0,,You're able to decide\Nwhether or not the war returns to Macondo!
Dialogue: 0,0:55:22.92,0:55:25.17,Default,,0,0,0,,Do you know how long\NI have waited for the moment
Dialogue: 0,0:55:25.25,0:55:28.00,Default,,0,0,0,,that I could finally\Ntake back Macondo for our cause?
Dialogue: 0,0:55:31.13,0:55:32.21,Default,,0,0,0,,No, I don't.
Dialogue: 0,0:55:36.21,0:55:37.67,Default,,0,0,0,,But I do know this much.
Dialogue: 0,0:55:39.13,0:55:41.51,Default,,0,0,0,,There is still time\Nfor you to do what is right.
Dialogue: 0,0:55:53.21,0:55:56.71,Default,,0,0,0,,VICTORY WILL BE FOUND IN THE FRAY
Dialogue: 0,0:55:58.75,0:56:00.29,Default,,0,0,0,,Faithful departed.
Dialogue: 0,0:56:00.38,0:56:04.51,Default,,0,0,0,,God the Son,\NRedeemer of the world, have mercy
Dialogue: 0,0:56:06.83,0:56:09.08,Default,,0,0,0,,on the souls of the faithful departed.
Dialogue: 0,0:56:09.17,0:56:10.46,Default,,0,0,0,,God the Holy Ghost…
Dialogue: 0,0:56:12.92,0:56:15.38,Default,,0,0,0,,have mercy on the souls\Nof the faithful departed.
Dialogue: 0,0:56:16.63,0:56:18.09,Default,,0,0,0,,Thou who holdest the keys,
Dialogue: 0,0:56:19.04,0:56:20.58,Default,,0,0,0,,Holy Trinity,
Dialogue: 0,0:56:20.67,0:56:24.00,Default,,0,0,0,,have mercy on the souls\Nof the faithful departed.
Dialogue: 0,0:56:27.54,0:56:31.25,Default,,0,0,0,,Holy Trinity, one God, have mercy\Non the souls of the faithful departed.
Dialogue: 0,0:56:31.92,0:56:34.46,Default,,0,0,0,,Have mercy on the souls\Nof the faithful departed.
Dialogue: 0,0:56:35.88,0:56:38.38,Default,,0,0,0,,Thou who holdest\Nthe keys to death and to Hell…
Dialogue: 0,0:56:40.42,0:56:41.75,Default,,0,0,0,,we ask for your mercy,
Dialogue: 0,0:57:01.63,0:57:04.59,Default,,0,0,0,,We didn't free ourselves of anything,\NJosé Arcadio Buendía.
Dialogue: 0,0:57:08.79,0:57:10.83,Default,,0,0,0,,We ended up raising a monster.
Dialogue: 0,0:57:10.92,0:57:13.92,Default,,0,0,0,,Attack now!
Dialogue: 0,0:57:20.25,0:57:22.50,Default,,0,0,0,,BASED ON THE NOVEL BY\NGABRIEL GARCÍA MÁRQUEZ
